## 10. Backend Requirements

### `/api/upload` (POST, multipart) — writes to `media.featheredsocial.site`

| Form field(s) | Mode | Response |
|---|---|---|
| `thumbnail`, `feed`, `original` | image bundle | `{ success, uploaded:{thumbnail:{url},feed:{url},original:{url}}, media_urls:{thumb,feed} }` |
| `file`, `filename`, `type`, `folder`, `timestamp` | single file | `{ success, url }` |

R2 bucket must serve from **`https://media.featheredsocial.site/`** (custom domain). All returned URLs must be absolute on this host.

### `/api/posts` (POST, JSON) — single insert for images AND videos

```sql
CREATE TABLE posts (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  content TEXT,
  media_url TEXT,
  media_type TEXT,             -- 'image' | 'video' | 'audio' | null
  media_urls TEXT,             -- JSON string of array
  media_types TEXT,            -- JSON string of array
  media_meta TEXT,             -- JSON string of array
  type TEXT,                   -- 'text' | 'image' | 'video' | 'audio'
  visibility TEXT DEFAULT 'public',
  location TEXT,
  feeling TEXT,
  tagged_users TEXT,           -- JSON string
  background TEXT,
  colours TEXT,
  background_style TEXT,
  link_preview TEXT,           -- JSON string
  song_name TEXT,
  song_id TEXT,
  audio_url TEXT,
  feed_key TEXT UNIQUE,
  reactions_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  comments_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  shares_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  views INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')),
  updated_at TEXT
);
```

Return `{ success: true, post: {...row} }`.

> ⚠️ **No `reel_id` column